From 271e133dd006820c2680aca171cb9d73daa2e2a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lucas Santos <lsantos7654@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Apr 2026 00:56:56 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 19/21] TUI presence stream + focus POST + sessions/subagents
 footer pills
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Wires the TUI into the per-client presence model:

  - SDKProvider generates a `clientID` UUID once per process and
    sends it as `X-Client-ID` on the SSE handshake (`/event`) and
    every `POST /event/focus`.
  - The SSE connection is the presence beacon — long-lived, one per
    process. The existing `startSSE` keep-alive loop is unchanged;
    when it dies, server-side `stream.onAbort` removes the entry.
  - A `createEffect` watching `route.data` POSTs the current
    sessionID (or null) on every navigation. A small `presenceReady`
    gate buffers the initial focus until the SSE handshake finishes,
    so the first POST never races ahead of the registration on the
    server.
  - Errors on the focus POST are swallowed — focus is best-effort
    metadata, not load-bearing.

Footer now shows two pills powered by `session.live.changed`:

    ●  N sessions      ●  N subagents

  - `roots = sessions.length - subagents.length`
  - `subagents = subagents.length`
  - Initial seed via `GET /global/live-sessions` on mount.
  - `Directory`, `Mcp`, and `Version` pills are dropped (the prior
    feedback that prompted patch 0027). `HivemindStatus` stays.
  - Same `View` rendered into both `home_footer` and `session_footer`
    slots so the pills are visible everywhere.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
